      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Parameters vs Hyperparameters and the Validation Set",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Parameters vs Hyperparameters",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Parameters",
                "Hyperparameters"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Set",
                  "**learned** from data in training",
                  "**set before** training"
                ],
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "weights, biases, tree split thresholds",
                  "learning rate, depth, regularisation strength, k"
                ],
                [
                  "Found by",
                  "gradient descent, closed form or greedy splits",
                  "==search==: loss not differentiable in them"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Three-Way Split",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Train",
                    "sub": "fit parameters",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Validation",
                    "sub": "choose hyperparameters",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Test",
                    "sub": "final report, once",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Typical split: ==60/20/20== or ==70/15/15==",
                "Tuning picks hyperparameters by ==validation score==",
                "Test set is touched ==once==, at the end, for an unbiased estimate"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not tune on the test set?** Repeated selection leaks test information; the score turns ==optimistically biased==",
                "**Role of the validation set?** A proxy for unseen data, used only to compare hyperparameter settings"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One look only",
              "text": "Look at the test set twice and it has become a validation set."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cross-Validation Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cross-Validation Workflow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. k-fold CV",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Split",
                    "sub": "k folds",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Train",
                    "sub": "k-1 folds",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "sub": "held-out fold",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rotate",
                    "sub": "k times",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Average",
                    "sub": "k scores",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Common choice: ==k=5== or ==k=10==",
                "==Leave-one-out== is k=n: nearly unbiased, {red:high variance}, very expensive",
                "Use LOO only for **tiny** datasets"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Splitters and Usage",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Splitter",
                "Use when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`StratifiedKFold`",
                  "classification: keeps class ratio"
                ],
                [
                  "`TimeSeriesSplit`",
                  "temporal: validation after training"
                ],
                [
                  "`GroupKFold`",
                  "rows share a group (patient, user)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "scores = cross_val_score(",
                "    model, X, y, cv=5, scoring='f1')",
                "scores.mean(), scores.std()"
              ],
              "note": "one score per fold; report mean and std"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Leakage Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Scaler, imputer or feature selection fitted on ==all data== before splitting leaks",
                "Wrap preprocessing and model in a ==Pipeline==: refit inside each fold"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why average k folds?** Reduces variance of the estimate",
                "**When is plain KFold wrong?** Imbalanced classes, time order, grouped rows",
                "**How does Pipeline stop leakage?** Preprocessing fits only on each fold's training part"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grid Search vs Random Search",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Grid Search vs Random Search",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Grid Search",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Grid== tries every combination of a discrete grid",
                "Cost multiplies: 3 x 4 x 5 = **60 configs**",
                "Fits = 60 x k folds, plus 1 refit on all training data"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Random Search",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Samples `n_iter` configs from distributions",
                "Bergstra and Bengio: beats grid when {green:few} hyperparameters matter",
                "Why: each trial tries a ==new value of every== hyperparameter; grid repeats values"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Sample",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "lr, C, alpha",
                  "**log** scale",
                  "`loguniform(1e-4, 1)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Integer (depth)",
                  "uniform",
                  "`randint(3, 15)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Usage and Mistakes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Both cross-validate every config, then ==refit== the best"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "GridSearchCV(est, param_grid, cv=5, scoring='f1', n_jobs=-1)",
                "RandomizedSearchCV(est, param_distributions,",
                "    n_iter=50, cv=5, random_state=0)",
                "s.best_params_, s.best_score_, s.cv_results_"
              ],
              "note": "read results after s.fit(X, y)"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Grid mistakes",
              "text": "Too fine wastes budget; too narrow misses the optimum. If `best_params_` sits on the **edge**, extend the range. Keep `refit=True`."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why random beats grid?** Few hyperparameters matter: more distinct values of each",
                "**Sampling scale?** Log for orders of magnitude"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bayesian Optimisation and Early Stopping",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Bayesian Optimisation and Early Stopping",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bayesian Optimisation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Surrogate== (Gaussian process or TPE) models score vs hyperparameters from past trials",
                "==Acquisition function== (expected improvement, UCB) picks the next trial",
                "It balances {purple:exploration} (uncertain regions) and {green:exploitation} (promising regions)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fit surrogate",
                    "note": "trials so far",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Maximise acquisition",
                    "note": "next config",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Evaluate",
                    "note": "train and score",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add result",
                    "note": "repeat",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Bayesian",
                "Random"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Trials",
                  "sequential",
                  "trivially parallel"
                ],
                [
                  "Best when",
                  "expensive (deep nets)",
                  "cheap; strong baseline"
                ],
                [
                  "Tools",
                  "Optuna (TPE), Hyperopt, scikit-optimize",
                  "RandomizedSearchCV"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Early Stopping",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Monitor ==validation loss== each epoch",
                "Stop after ==patience== epochs with no improvement; restore best weights",
                "Regularises, saves compute, tunes the epoch count automatically"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "X_tr, X_te, y_tr, y_te = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.2)",
                "es = EarlyStopping(patience=10, restore_best_weights=True)",
                "model.fit(X_tr, y_tr, validation_split=0.2,",
                "          epochs=200, callbacks=[es])",
                "model.evaluate(X_te, y_te)"
              ],
              "note": "test set split off first, used once"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Patience too small stops on ==noise==",
                "Rule: split off a ==test set== first and evaluate on it once",
                "Reason: validation data picks the epoch, so its score is biased",
                "Optuna pruners (`MedianPruner`) can kill bad trials early"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Nested Cross-Validation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Nested Cross-Validation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Bias Problem",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Best search CV score is ==optimistically biased==",
                "Same folds both **select** and **score** the model"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Nested Loops",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Outer split",
                    "sub": "5 folds",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Inner search",
                    "sub": "3 folds, full tuning",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Score",
                    "sub": "outer test fold, unseen",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "inner = GridSearchCV(est, grid, cv=3)",
                "scores = cross_val_score(inner, X, y, cv=5)"
              ],
              "note": "scores.mean() = honest estimate, search included"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Outer loop ==estimates== performance",
                "Inner loop ==selects== hyperparameters"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cost and Final Model",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Item",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fits",
                  "outer_k x (inner_k x configs + 1 refit)"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "5 x (3 x 20 + 1) = **305 fits**"
                ],
                [
                  "Cheaper",
                  "random search or smaller inner loop"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Estimate, not a model",
              "text": "Afterwards run the search ==once on all training data== to get the deployed model. Only comparing configs? Plain CV."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
